/**
@mainpage OpenCaliper developer reference

OpenCaliper reads recorded signals into a shared Python data model, performs
numerical analysis, and presents time and frequency plots in a Qt desktop GUI.
This reference is generated from the checked-in Python source and docstrings.

@section start_here Start here

- @ref architecture : component drawings, ownership and loading sequence.
- opencaliper.core.Signal and opencaliper.core.Recording : shared data model.
- opencaliper.core.load() and opencaliper.core.export() : format entry points.
- opencaliper.analysis : FFT, explicit resampling, statistics and cursor interpolation.
- opencaliper.processing : expressions, filters, alignment, events and spectrograms.
- opencaliper.converterscripts.convert : shared format dispatcher.
- opencaliper.workspace.WorkspaceMixin : archives and structural undo.
- opencaliper.tools.ToolsMixin : processing dialogs and plot export.
- opencaliper.gui.Window : desktop interaction controller.
- scripts.launch.main() : first-run setup and launch.
- run_opencaliper.main() : direct GUI launch in the selected environment.

Use the Packages, Classes and Files navigation to inspect definitions and their
source. Class diagrams show relationships Doxygen can infer. Python is dynamic,
so inferred relationships are incomplete; the curated architecture drawings
explain runtime ownership explicitly.

@section guides Reading alongside the reference

The repository's `docs/README.md` is the documentation index. Read
`docs/USER_GUIDE.md` for application use, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for the extended
architecture explanation, `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` for an executable API walkthrough
and test map, `docs/MAT_FORMAT.md` for MAT/ESRP layouts,
`docs/PYTHON_API.md` for data/processing APIs, `docs/COMMAND_LINE.md` for terminal
usage and `docs/WORKSPACE_FORMAT.md` for persisted state. The adapter contract
and extension example live in `opencaliper/converterscripts/README.md`.
The source checkout also contains `examples/example.py` and its synthetic MAT
file. Private `measFiles/`, environments, tests and generated exports are not
inputs to this documentation build.

@section maintenance Maintaining this reference

Document parameters, units, return values, constraints and side effects next
to the function they describe. Build with `doxygen Doxyfile` from the project
root and inspect `docs-api/html/index.html`. See `docs/DOXYGEN.md` for setup
and writing conventions. Documentation generation imports no application code.
*/
